  "counterinterpretations_and_limits": [
    "The parenthetical could be read as all reporting parameters or only report-bit fields. The original metadata-only finite caption query and absence of all/every do not require either narrowing or whole-topic recall. Actual 38.214 reporting clauses connect the six resource-mapping/port-combination rows to reported CSI, so they are not admitted merely from a CSI token.",
    "A human may deduplicate repeated specNumber/tableNumber pairs. The preserved original graph has release-qualified Table identities, and its specific original query returns one row per matched Table path without DISTINCT and explicitly LIMIT20. The contract therefore preserves that authored row multiplicity while not inventing an unrequested release field. This is a finite retained metadata list, not a unique cross-release catalog.",
    "A broader title-based predicate admits a real PMI parameter table before the cutoff. That true alternative disproves an all-topic completeness claim, but it does not invalidate a finite list of relevant examples, nor prove mandatory clarification. The old local clarification recommendation was never ROOT-sealed and is superseded only in that overstrong implication.",
    "Captions and Section numbers provide useful optional context but are not independently required by the request to list tables. Spec number and table number identify the named tables. All four original native columns are nevertheless compared with independent SQL; this does not certify complete table cells, equations, rendering, or full CSI implementation."
  ],
